ing":"**Identifying doc and code contradictions**\n\n**Outlining risk register and onboarding plan**\n\n**Separating package markers from business modules**\n\n**Drafting file generation script**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_04f44e1e3b36ae1e016a95878ed1a087d28ae6c9c433b4bacc\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Identifying doc and code contradictions**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Outlining risk register and onboarding plan**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Separating package markers from business modules**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Drafting file generation script**\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"I’ve mapped the repo. Next I’m writing the five files under `/workspace/out` from the fixture code only.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_04f44e1e3b36ae1e016a958798e42c87d2b0b1d1bbabc4d6d1\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_JjSdAdYhMSxw4xVUagBc8UuQ|fc_04f44e1e3b36ae1e016a958799576487d29aa2667d7c4feacf","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/out/module_map.json","content":"{\n  \"modules\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"minisvc.cli\",\n      \"path\": \"minisvc/cli.py\",\n      \"purpose\": \"CLI bootstrap entry point that loads settings, opens the repository, initializes schema, and prints readiness.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"minisvc.config\",\n      \"path\": \"minisvc/config.py\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Loads runtime settings from environment variables into an immutable Settings dataclass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"minisvc.models\",\n      \"path\": \"minisvc/models.py\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Defines the core Order data model shared by API, audit, and storage code.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"minisvc.audit\",\n      \"path\": \"minisvc/audit.py\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Builds audit event payload dictionaries from Order objects; it does not persist them.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\",\n      \"path\": \"minisvc/api/handlers.py\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Implements request handlers for creating and fetching orders.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"minisvc.api.routes\",\n      \"path\": \"minisvc/api/routes.py\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Registers HTTP routes on an external app object by binding handler lambdas to a repository instance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\",\n      \"path\": \"minisvc/storage/repo.py\",\n      \"purpose\": \"SQLite-backed repository for schema creation, order inserts, and order reads.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"entry_points\": [\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n      \"kind\": \"cli\",\n      \"source\": \"pyproject.toml [project.scripts]\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\",\n      \"kind\": \"http_route_registration\",\n      \"source\": \"minisvc/api/routes.py\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n      \"kind\": \"http_handler\",\n      \"source\": \"minisvc/api/handlers.py\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n      \"kind\": \"http_handler\",\n      \"source\": \"minisvc/api/handlers.py\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"dependency_edges\": [\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.cli\", \"to\": \"minisvc.config\", \"type\": \"imports\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\", \"to\": \"minisvc.config:load_settings\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\", \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository\", \"type\": \"instantiates\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\", \"to\": \"environment:MINISVC_DB\", \"type\": \"reads_config\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\", \"to\": \"environment:MINISVC_READONLY\", \"type\": \"reads_config\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.cli\", \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\", \"type\": \"imports\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\", \"to\": \"minisvc.models\", \"type\": \"imports\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\", \"to\": \"sqlite:orders\", \"type\": \"persists_to\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\", \"to\": \"sqlite:orders\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.init_schema\", \"to\": \"sqlite:orders\", \"type\": \"persists_to\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\", \"to\": \"minisvc.audit\", \"type\": \"imports\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\", \"to\": \"minisvc.models\", \"type\": \"imports\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\", \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\", \"type\": \"imports\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\", \"to\": \"minisvc.models:Order\", \"type\": \"instantiates\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\", \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\", \"to\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\", \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\", \"to\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.routes\", \"to\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\", \"type\": \"imports\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\", \"to\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\", \"to\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.audit\", \"to\": \"minisvc.models\", \"type\": \"imports\"}\n  ],\n  \"key_functions\": [\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n      \"summary\": \"Service bootstrap. Loads Settings from os.environ, builds OrderRepository with the configured database path, creates the orders table if needed, then prints a ready message.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"argv=None\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"int exit code 0\"],\n      \"side_effects\": [\"reads environment\", \"creates SQLite orders table if missing\", \"writes stdout\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.config:load_settings\",\n      \"summary\": \"Maps MINISVC_DB and MINISVC_READONLY environment variables into a frozen Settings value.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"env dict[str, str]\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"Settings(database_path, readonly)\"],\n      \"side_effects\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.init_schema\",\n      \"summary\": \"Creates the orders table if it does not exist.\",\n      \"inputs\": [],\n      \"outputs\": [],\n      \"side_effects\": [\"opens SQLite connection\", \"executes DDL\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\",\n      \"summary\": \"Inserts one Order row into SQLite with no retry, no readonly gate, and no duplicate handling.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"Order\"],\n      \"outputs\": [],\n      \"side_effects\": [\"opens SQLite connection\", \"executes INSERT into orders\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\",\n      \"summary\": \"Reads one order row by order_id and returns an Order or None.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"order_id str\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"Order | None\"],\n      \"side_effects\": [\"opens SQLite connection\", \"executes SELECT from orders\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n      \"summary\": \"Builds an Order from payload fields, saves it through the repository, and returns a created response with an inline audit event dict.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"payload dict\", \"OrderRepository\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"response dict\"],\n      \"side_effects\": [\"casts total_cents to int\", \"writes order to SQLite via repo.save\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n      \"summary\": \"Fetches an order, returns missing when absent, or returns the order data plus an inline read audit event.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"order_id str\", \"OrderRepository\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"response dict\"],\n      \"side_effects\": [\"reads SQLite via repo.get\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\",\n      \"summary\": \"Binds POST /orders and GET /orders/<order_id> handlers onto an app object using lambdas that close over the repository.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"app\", \"repo\"],\n      \"outputs\": [],\n      \"side_effects\": [\"mutates external app route table\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\",\n      \"summary\": \"Formats a small audit-style dict for order actions. It is pure and does not write to storage.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"Order\", \"action str\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"dict\"],\n      \"side_effects\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"runtime_flows\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"CLI startup flow\",\n      \"steps\": [\n        \"The `minisvc` console script resolves to `minisvc.cli:main` from `pyproject.toml`.\",\n        \"`main` calls `minisvc.config.load_settings(os.environ)` to read `MINISVC_DB` and `MINISVC_READONLY`.\",\n        \"`main` instantiates `minisvc.storage.repo.OrderRepository(settings.database_path)`.\",\n        \"`main` calls `repo.init_schema()` to create the `orders` table if missing.\",\n        \"`main` prints `minisvc ready at ...` and exits with status code 0.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"HTTP create-order flow\",\n      \"steps\": [\n        \"An external HTTP app calls `minisvc.api.routes.register_routes(app, repo)` during setup.\",\n        \"`register_routes` binds POST `/orders` to a lambda that calls `minisvc.api.handlers.create_order(payload, repo)`.\",\n        \"`create_order` reads `order_id`, `customer`, and `total_cents` from the payload and builds a `minisvc.models.Order`.\",\n        \"`create_order` calls `repo.save(order)`.\",\n        \"`OrderRepository.save` opens SQLite and inserts the order row into the `orders` table.\",\n        \"Control returns to `create_order`, which builds an inline event with `minisvc.audit.order_event(order, \\\"created\\\")`.\",\n        \"The handler returns `{status: \\\"created\\\", order_id: ..., event: ...}` to the HTTP adapter.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"HTTP get-order flow\",\n      \"steps\": [\n        \"`register_routes` binds GET `/orders/<order_id>` to a lambda that calls `minisvc.api.handlers.get_order(order_id, repo)`.\",\n        \"`get_order` calls `repo.get(order_id)`.\",\n        \"`OrderRepository.get` runs a SQLite SELECT and returns an `Order` or `None`.\",\n        \"If the order is missing, the handler returns `{status: \\\"missing\\\", order_id: ...}`.\",\n        \"If found, the handler returns `{status: \\\"ok\\\", order: order.__dict__, event: order_event(order, \\\"read\\\")}`.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":278,"output":3352,"cacheRead":19456,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":544,"totalTokens":23086,"cost":{"input":0.0006950000000000001,"output":0.05028,"cacheRead":0.004863999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.055839}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788184461753,"responseId":"resp_04f44e1e3b36ae1e016a95878e1a3487d28f802c17c92decac","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_JjSdAdYhMSxw4xVUagBc8UuQ|fc_04f44e1e3b36ae1e016a958799576487d29aa2667d7c4feacf","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[out/module_map.json#DDDE]\nSuccessfully wrote 8939 bytes to /workspace/out/module_map.json"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/module_map.json"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788184523296},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ATbfIdRBGKeJOEY12rGlqb4q|fc_04f44e1e3b36ae1e016a9587cc991c87d28241ddaa515884b2","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/out/architecture.md","content":"# minisvc architecture summary\n\n## What this repo is\n`minisvc` is a small Python service skeleton with two live runtime surfaces:\n- a CLI bootstrap command at `minisvc.cli:main`\n- HTTP route registration at `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes`\n\nIt stores orders in SQLite through one repository class. The repo has no built-in web server module; an outside app object must call `register_routes(app, repo)`.\n\nDo not treat these files as business logic:\n- `minisvc/__init__.py`\n- `minisvc/api/__init__.py`\n- `minisvc/storage/__init__.py`\n\nThey are package markers or export stubs only.\n\n## Main modules\n- `minisvc/config.py` — loads `MINISVC_DB` and `MINISVC_READONLY` into `Settings`\n- `minisvc/models.py` — defines the `Order` dataclass\n- `minisvc/storage/repo.py` — owns SQLite schema setup, inserts, and reads\n- `minisvc/audit.py` — formats audit event dicts; it does not save them\n- `minisvc/api/handlers.py` — core create/get order logic\n- `minisvc/api/routes.py` — wires handlers into an external HTTP adapter\n- `minisvc/cli.py` — startup path for local bootstrap\n\n## Entry points\n- `minisvc.cli:main` — exposed as the `minisvc` console script in `pyproject.toml`\n- `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes` — API setup entry point for an external app\n- Handler entry points used by the HTTP adapter:\n  - `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order`\n  - `minisvc.api.handlers:get_order`\n\n## Data flow\n### CLI startup flow\n1. `minisvc.cli:main` reads env through `load_settings(os.environ)`.\n2. It builds `OrderRepository(settings.database_path)`.\n3. It calls `repo.init_schema()`.\n4. The repository creates the `orders` table if needed.\n5. The CLI prints the ready path and exits.\n\n### HTTP create-order flow\n1. An outside app calls `register_routes(app, repo)`.\n2. `register_routes` binds POST `/orders` to `create_order(payload, repo)`.\n3. `create_order` builds an `Order` from `payload[\"order_id\"]`, `payload[\"customer\"]`, and `int(payload[\"total_cents\"])`.\n4. It calls `repo.save(order)`.\n5. `OrderRepository.save` opens SQLite and inserts one row into `orders`.\n6. The handler returns a response dict with status, order id, and an inline event from `order_event(order, \"created\")`.\n\n### HTTP get-order flow\n1. GET `/orders/<order_id>` calls `get_order(order_id, repo)`.\n2. The handler calls `repo.get(order_id)`.\n3. The repository reads from SQLite and returns `Order` or `None`.\n4. The handler returns either `{\"status\": \"missing\"}` or `{\"status\": \"ok\", \"order\": ..., \"event\": ...}`.\n\n## Storage\n- Storage backend: SQLite via `sqlite3` in `minisvc/storage/repo.py`\n- File path source: `MINISVC_DB`, default `orders.sqlite`\n- Schema: one table, `orders(order_id text primary key, customer text not null, total_cents integer not null)`\n- Audit storage: none in code. Audit data is only a returned dict from `minisvc.audit.order_event`\n\n## Config and runtime behavior\n- `MINISVC_DB` sets the SQLite file path\n- `MINISVC_READONLY` is parsed into `Settings.readonly`\n- No live code uses `Settings.readonly` after config load\n- No retry loop wraps `repo.save`\n- No app factory, dependency injection container, or transaction wrapper exists beyond per-call SQLite context managers\n\n## Risks and extension points\n### Risks\n- Readonly mode is documented but not enforced. Write paths still call `repo.save`.\n- Create-order has no payload validation beyond direct key access and `int(...)` casting. Bad input raises exceptions.\n- Audit events are not durable. They are response data only.\n- Each repository method opens its own SQLite connection. There is no retry, no busy timeout setup, and no explicit concurrency strategy.\n- The default DB path is relative (`orders.sqlite`), so runtime location depends on the current working directory.\n\n### Good extension points\n- `minisvc.api.handlers.create_order` is the place to add input checks, readonly gating, and richer error mapping.\n- `minisvc.storage.repo.OrderRepository` is the place to add audit tables, retries, transaction policy, and migrations.\n- `minisvc.api.routes.register_routes` is the place to swap lambdas for named adapter functions if the HTTP layer grows.\n- `minisvc.config.load_settings` is the place to add new env-driven settings.\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":3661,"output":1133,"cacheRead":19456,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":24250,"cost":{"input":0.009152500000000001,"output":0.016995,"cacheRead":0.004863999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0310115}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788184523299,"responseId":"resp_04f44e1e3b36ae1e016a9587cbbf3487d287b6eb80631dd935","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ATbfIdRBGKeJOEY12rGlqb4q|fc_04f44e1e3b36ae1e016a9587cc991c87d28241ddaa515884b2","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[out/architecture.md#3435]\nSuccessfully wrote 4191 bytes to /workspace/out/architecture.md"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/architecture.md"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788184544955},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_wRZ6hstO6dxXfABXhXrJTa0G|fc_04f44e1e3b36ae1e016a9587e2a80087d28b9cf768fa20b5b5","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv","content":"claim,doc_source,code_evidence,assessment,risk\n\"MINISVC_READONLY=1 blocks all write paths\",\"README.md lines 5-8 design notes\",\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 parses readonly into Settings; minisvc/cli.py:8-10 and minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 never check settings.readonly; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 always inserts\",\"contradicted\",\"Operators may think write protection is on when order creation still writes to SQLite.\"\n\"create_order retries failed SQLite writes twice before returning an error response\",\"README.md lines 5-8 design notes\",\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 calls repo.save once; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 performs one INSERT with no retry loop or error handling\",\"contradicted\",\"Transient SQLite failures will surface at once and may break request handling.\"\n\"Audit events are stored in a durable audit table\",\"README.md lines 5-8 design notes\",\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 returns an in-memory dict only; minisvc/storage/repo.py schema and writes touch only the orders table\",\"contradicted\",\"Teams may rely on an audit trail that the service does not persist.\"\n\"This service accepts orders through a small HTTP adapter and a CLI bootstrap command\",\"README.md lines 1-4\",\"pyproject.toml:6-7 exposes minisvc.cli:main; minisvc/api/routes.py:4-6 registers HTTP routes for order create/read\",\"confirmed\",\"Low; high-level shape matches code.\"\n\"The fixture code is authoritative when docs and implementation disagree\",\"README.md line 10\",\"Repository behavior matches this instruction because the documented older design notes conflict with current code\",\"confirmed\",\"Low; use code over docs during maintenance.\"\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1241,"output":407,"cacheRead":23040,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":24688,"cost":{"input":0.0031025000000000002,"output":0.006105,"cacheRead":0.0057599999999999995,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0149675}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788184544957,"responseId":"resp_04f44e1e3b36ae1e016a9587e1626487d29d69756a59c50782","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_wRZ6hstO6dxXfABXhXrJTa0G|fc_04f44e1e3b36ae1e016a9587e2a80087d28b9cf768fa20b5b5","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv#8361]\nSuccessfully wrote 1613 bytes to /workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788184553920},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_rXV1O43bkgsRgaoLNerMtHX0|fc_04f44e1e3b36ae1e016a9587eb51c087d2a3e27145ac1318e2","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/out/risk_register.csv","content":"risk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint\nR1,storage/data durability,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 inserts directly into SQLite with one per-call connection and no retry or busy-timeout setup\",\"Transient file-lock or I/O issues can fail writes at once and lose requests unless the caller retries\",\"Add bounded retry and error mapping around writes; consider sqlite timeout or busy handling and request-level tests\",\"storage owner\"\nR2,audit behavior,\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 creates dict payloads only; minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-29 defines and uses only the orders table\",\"No durable audit trail exists for created or read events\",\"Add an audit table plus repository methods or a transaction-aware audit sink\",\"service owner\"\nR3,configuration/runtime environment,\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 defaults MINISVC_DB to relative path orders.sqlite; minisvc/cli.py:8-11 uses it as-is\",\"Database location changes with process working directory and can create data in the wrong place\",\"Require an absolute configured path in deployed environments or resolve relative paths from a known app root\",\"ops owner\"\nR4,configuration/runtime environment,\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 parses MINISVC_READONLY, but no caller uses Settings.readonly\",\"Operators can set readonly and still allow writes, which breaks safety expectations\",\"Enforce readonly in create paths or repository save methods and add a test for it\",\"service owner\"\nR5,API input validation,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:7-10 reads payload keys directly and casts total_cents with int(...)\",\"Missing keys or bad types will raise exceptions instead of returning controlled client errors\",\"Add schema validation and explicit 4xx error responses at the handler or adapter boundary\",\"api owner\"\nR6,API/storage error handling,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:12 and minisvc/storage/repo.py:18-22 do not catch sqlite3.IntegrityError or other DB exceptions\",\"Duplicate order IDs or DB failures likely bubble up as unhandled errors\",\"Translate storage exceptions into stable API responses and add duplicate-id coverage\",\"api owner\"\nR7,startup/schema lifecycle,\"minisvc/cli.py:9-10 runs init_schema only in the CLI path; API route registration does not ensure schema exists\",\"An HTTP deployment that skips CLI bootstrap can hit missing-table failures on first request\",\"Move schema init into app startup or repository construction used by the HTTP stack\",\"runtime owner\"\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":663,"output":545,"cacheRead":24064,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":25272,"cost":{"input":0.0016575000000000001,"output":0.008175,"cacheRead":0.006016,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0158485}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788184553922,"responseId":"resp_04f44e1e3b36ae1e016a9587ea6ee887d2960da9bb7a7ae005","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_rXV1O43bkgsRgaoLNerMtHX0|fc_04f44e1e3b36ae1e016a9587eb51c087d2a3e27145ac1318e2","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[out/risk_register.csv#BD46]\nSuccessfully wrote 2397 bytes to /workspace/out/risk_register.csv"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/risk_register.csv"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788184565115},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0O1uPBvjv2qCmw84pFVujwJ5|fc_04f44e1e3b36ae1e016a9587f6586c87d289d93bdeef9f3fd1","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md","content":"# New engineer onboarding plan\n\n## What to read first\n1. `README.md` — read the repo promise, but expect code to win where notes are old.\n2. `pyproject.toml` — see the console entry point `minisvc.cli:main`.\n3. `minisvc/cli.py` — shortest live startup path.\n4. `minisvc/config.py` — runtime settings and env names.\n5. `minisvc/storage/repo.py` — SQLite schema, writes, and reads.\n6. `minisvc/api/handlers.py` — business flow for create/read.\n7. `minisvc/api/routes.py` — adapter wiring.\n8. `minisvc/audit.py` and `minisvc/models.py` — small support code.\n\n## Active runtime code vs simple files\n### Active runtime code\n- `minisvc/cli.py`\n- `minisvc/config.py`\n- `minisvc/storage/repo.py`\n- `minisvc/api/handlers.py`\n- `minisvc/api/routes.py`\n- `minisvc/audit.py`\n- `minisvc/models.py`\n\n### Package marker or dead-simple files\n- `minisvc/__init__.py` — export stub only\n- `minisvc/api/__init__.py` — empty package marker\n- `minisvc/storage/__init__.py` — empty package marker\n\n## Local run commands\nFrom the repo root:\n- Bootstrap the CLI path:\n  - `python3 -c 'from minisvc.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())'`\n- Run with a chosen DB path:\n  - `MINISVC_DB=/tmp/minisvc.sqlite python3 -c 'from minisvc.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())'`\n- Quick import sanity check:\n  - `python3 -m compileall minisvc`\n- Quick create/read trace in one process:\n  - `python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom minisvc.storage.repo import OrderRepository\nfrom minisvc.api.handlers import create_order, get_order\nrepo = OrderRepository('/tmp/minisvc-dev.sqlite')\nrepo.init_schema()\nprint(create_order({'order_id': 'o1', 'customer': 'Ada', 'total_cents': 1200}, repo))\nprint(get_order('o1', repo))\nPY`\n\n## First breakpoint or trace point\nStart at `minisvc/api/handlers.py:create_order`.\n- It is the best first stop because it shows payload parsing, model creation, persistence, and audit-event creation in one short path.\n- If you want lower-level storage detail, step next into `minisvc/storage/repo.py:save`.\n\n## Two safe first changes\n1. Add a small test or guard for readonly mode around `create_order` or `OrderRepository.save`.\n   - Safe because the setting already exists in `config.py` but is not enforced.\n2. Add input validation for `order_id`, `customer`, and `total_cents` in `create_order`.\n   - Safe because current code already depends on those fields and fails hard on bad payloads.\n\n## What to keep in mind\n- The HTTP app object is outside this repo.\n- Audit events are returned in responses, not stored.\n- The README design notes do not match all current behavior, so check the code before you change anything.\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":731,"output":773,"cacheRead":24576,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":26080,"cost":{"input":0.0018275000000000001,"output":0.011595000000000001,"cacheRead":0.006144,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0195665}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788184565119,"responseId":"resp_04f44e1e3b36ae1e016a9587f57bf887d28bff15379bb86402","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_0O1uPBvjv2qCmw84pFVujwJ5|fc_04f44e1e3b36ae1e016a9587f6586c87d289d93bdeef9f3fd1","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[out/onboarding_plan.md#0275]\nSuccessfully wrote 2602 bytes to /workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788184580237},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning JSON validation and preview**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_04f44e1e3b36ae1e016a95880555e487d288eafe3db2813915\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning JSON validation and preview**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_1eGl5ZlQCrBhpXzew9MEXHmb|fc_04f44e1e3b36ae1e016a95880637d887d2b77183d0b1c43513","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, csv, pathlib\nbase = pathlib.Path('/workspace/out')\njson.load(open(base/'module_map.json'))\nfor name in ['doc_code_discrepancies.csv','risk_register.csv']:\n    with open(base/name, newline='') as f:\n        rows=list(csv.reader(f))\n        print(name, len(rows)-1)\nprint('ok')\nPY","timeout":20}}],"api":